# Hual02 route (item59, re-authored by item67/item67f/item67g): player input from the vent
# spawn to Carrington's cell and the exit plateau, objectives driven only by the game's own
# chains.
#
# Player input (no set_goal/take_control): crouch-crawl through the ceiling vent
# (spawn 104,1840,-4536 -> gallery), two aimed shots break the two grates
# (BreakableMover5 at 104,1192 yaw 270; BreakAbleMover2 at -496,-688 yaw 259.5,
# measured legs 9-12), crawl the duct and drop into the office floor -4856,
# walk the underfloor to the service lift lobby (the corridor's Porte11 is opened
# by real input: the game's Grab tail -> Porte11.PlayerTrigger), ride the lift (item67:
# the game's own LiftButton0.PlayerTrigger -> LiftManager states -> LiftCage key move;
# the player is carried by the decoded mover-base attachment), then walk out of the floor-2
# cage through the live `LiftDoor1` doorway and follow the map's own surface ReachSpec/PathNode
# chain to the depot reader (item67g). Only the locked `Porte19` gap and the later isolated
# segments are labelled teleports.
#
# item67f: the doorway is not `Porte20`. Hual02's `Porte4`/`Porte20` (`XIDCine.Porte`, Tags
# 'porte_bas'/'porte_haut') are serialised `bDeleteMe=true` in a trailing block of 54 destroyed
# exports (with the LiftManager's stale XIIIMover0 cage reference); the engine's
# `AActor::IsPendingKill` reports them dead, so they are not part of the live level. No actor in
# the map fires an event named 'porte_haut'/'porte_bas' (the strings occur only as the live
# `LiftDoor` Tags), and the LiftManager's automatic radius search only matches `XIDCine.LiftDoor`.
# The live floor-2 exit is `LiftDoor1`, which the manager's own outer-door states open.
#
# Labelled diagnostic: the hostile BaseSoldier* pawns are removed by the test
# (remove_soldiers). Under the real level clock the unmodified level's underfloor
# gauntlet (BaseSoldier26 (-1714.7,894.9), BaseSoldier27 (-2218.2,698.9, shotgun +
# grenades), BaseSoldier25 (-1923.3,-1094.1), lobby BaseSoldier15/28, upper
# BaseSoldier14) kills the unarmoured player at t~130-138 near (-1834,773)..
# (-1663,1146) (measured; crouching does not save the player). That kill is the
# pinned next blocker for playing this level through.
#
# Labelled teleports, each for a measured movement gap (see the report):
# - "depot"          t=402 (-8880,722): after the ride the walker leaves the cage through the
#                    live `LiftDoor1` and follows the map's own nav chain (item67g) across the
#                    surface to the reader (MagneticPassTrigger1 at -5259,803; touched at
#                    t=396.2, used by real input at t=400.5: aim-focus
#                    TargetActor=MagneticPassTrigger1, bCanTrigger=true, Grab runs). With no
#                    magnetic card, Porte19 (Tag 'Porteentrevs') stays locked, so the teleport
#                    crosses it. The card pickup (Hual02MagneticCardPick4 at -3474,1550) sits in
#                    the petitesalle card room: its entrance Porte21 (Event 'reveil_3') opens by
#                    real `use` from the neighbouring zone, but that zone (the office + card
#                    room nav island, 71 PathNodes) is walled off from the surface corridor
#                    except the two shootable `grande_vitre` window panes (StaticMeshActor8 at
#                    -4328,1638 and StaticMeshActor7 at -3354,1632, the map's only ColCategory-3
#                    blocking meshes; item67j). The glass now shatters on bullet impact
#                    (item67j engine rule, unit-tested), but the aperture is z -112..16 (sill
#                    112 UU above the walked floors) and no measured retail primitive crosses it
#                    from the flat corridor floor (step 35 = Engine.dll stepUp 0x104829c4;
#                    jump 92.8 = JumpZ 420 with PhysicsVolume.Gravity (0,0,-950); no sill-mantle
#                    script in any package), so the card stays unreachable on foot - pinned.
#                    item67j measured the rest of the chain with the card in hand (the committed
#                    probe opt_in_hual02_card_room_reader_chain): the reader use with the card
#                    fires OutEvent 'Porteentrevs' and Porte19 opens, but the corridor west of
#                    Porte19 then pins at x~-6198 against PorteDecors18/19 - decor doors whose
#                    PorteDecors.SetInitialState forces ForeverLocked (its PlayerTrigger only
#                    plays a sound), so the teleport also crosses that seal.
# - "prison entry"   t=408 (-10368,2800): the prison compound perimeter is sealed
#                    in this sim (Porte151 Locked opens only from Carrington's
#                    escort moveseq); the landing touches DetectionVolume14 whose
#                    'didact6' event completes goal 2 through XIIIGoalTrigger1.
# - "prison grille escape" t=414 (-10176,2900): the DV14 landing sits inside the
#                    simplified collision of StaticMeshActor1024 'grille_prison';
#                    measured leg31: the player is pinned until moved.
# - "stair head"     t=462 (-14896,656,438): the exit stairwell pins the walker at
#                    (-14078,1314,35) (measured legs 20-23); the corridor beyond is
#                    sealed by the Locked Porte151, so the exit plateau is entered here.
#
# Weapon grant (labelled diagnostic): the player would carry the Beretta from
# Hual01b (the campaign loadout; Hual01a's route test documents no grant because
# the fresh-login inventory already has it). Starting on Hual02 directly hands the
# Fists only, so the route re-grants xiii.Beretta to make the two grate shots real.
#
# Objectives completed by the game's chains on this route (measured legs 31-37 and the
# fixture runs): goals 4/5/6 complete (the anti-goal completions), goal 3 promoted by the
# depot reader chain (MagneticPassTrigger1 -> Grab) but not completed. The promotion chain
# for goals 1 and 2 is blocked in this sim: DetectionVolume21 ('demarre_bureau', which
# promotes goal 1 through XIIIGoalTrigger3) floats 78 UU above the real duct floor
# (z=-4320, cylinder half-height 40, measured), and the eavesdrop scene's
# 'Blam' -> 'objectif92' promotion of goal 2 stalls at the unimplemented CWndSFXTrigger
# scene action. The DV14 -> 'didact6' -> XIIIGoalTrigger1 completion of goal 2 only
# validates a promoted goal (measured: leg37 with the diagnostic cue vs the fixture).
# (TouchTrigger8 z=63 gallery -> Cine7 'soldat_plan' raid -> 'soldat_assome' ->
# CineTrigger8 CineGoto -> Carrington moveseqs open Porte151 -> 'fin') is blocked:
# TouchTrigger8's gallery and Porte151 are both unreachable on foot in this sim, so
# goal 0 and the travel request stay unmet; the test asserts that measured blocker.
t=0.20 crouch 1
t=0.50 goto 104 1840 -4536
t=3.00 goto 104 1730 -4536
t=8.00 goto 104 1400 -4536
t=12.00 yaw 270
t=12.50 grant xiii.Beretta
t=14.00 fire
t=20.00 goto 104 1128 -4536
t=26.00 goto -200 1128 -4536
t=34.00 goto -424 1128 -4536
t=38.00 goto -424 -300 -4536
t=52.00 yaw 259.5
t=53.00 fire
t=55.00 fire
t=58.00 goto -424 -680 -4536
t=64.00 goto -560 -688 -4536
t=72.00 crouch 0
t=78.00 goto -713 -517 -4781
t=86.00 goto -711 -18 -4781
t=94.00 goto -1004 321 -4781
t=100.00 goto -1394 305 -4781
t=106.00 goto -1396 16 -4781
